                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1d52d3f6-b54e-398d-899a-3215ef656bc7",
                        "entry_id": "99a99940-416d-3db4-bbf0-4ee553729e6c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Scientifique spécialiste de l’étude des chauves-souris, également connue sous le nom de chiroptérologie."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ebb54ca6-2a07-48d8-abaa-3a016d873e23",
                                "sense_id": "1d52d3f6-b54e-398d-899a-3215ef656bc7",
                                "text": "Des soirées de capture au filet ont réuni nos chiroptérologues : un Vespertilion de Daubenton (mâle), une Pipistrelle de Kuhl (femelle post-lactante) et un Vespertilion de Bechstein (femelle post-lactante) ont été capturés."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2b496945-57b5-458a-8b9e-0ff6da3f0b57",
                                "sense_id": "1d52d3f6-b54e-398d-899a-3215ef656bc7",
                                "text": "En cas de découverte d’une chauve-souris morte, blessée, affaiblie ou qui présente des difficultés à voler, il est recommandé de ne pas la toucher, de ne pas la ramasser et de prévenir un vétérinaire ou un chiroptérologue, c’est-à-dire un spécialiste de cet animal."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cc899beb-8e62-4bd1-8f93-4f2b9dd72076",
                                "sense_id": "1d52d3f6-b54e-398d-899a-3215ef656bc7",
                                "text": "« Nous y avons repéré quatre espèces : la pipistrelle de Nathusius, la noctule commune, la sérotine bicolore et la noctule de Leisler », affirme Thomas Deana, chiroptérologue à la ligue pour la protection des oiseaux (LPO)."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f3d203d0-54a8-4e77-afec-a7d3b08d45f0",
                        "source_entry_id": "99a99940-416d-3db4-bbf0-4ee553729e6c",
                        "source_sense_id": "1d52d3f6-b54e-398d-899a-3215ef656bc7",
                        "target_lang_word": "chiropterologist",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "chiropterologist",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6f0792d4-7f8a-377e-a444-d6ee85fa69f3",
                                        "entry_id": "00353299-e909-3aaf-bd96-502bbae90015",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone who studies bats (the flying mammals)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "524b6fd6-20b2-4313-ae20-95bbf81e8272",
                                                "sense_id": "6f0792d4-7f8a-377e-a444-d6ee85fa69f3",
                                                "text": "Several years later, after reading three of his books on bats, I placed a call to the venerable chiropterologist Dr. M. Brock Fenton, known as the \"batman\" of York University in Toronto."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "18315ef8-bf1f-4a9d-866d-2d36dd8459f4",
                                                "sense_id": "6f0792d4-7f8a-377e-a444-d6ee85fa69f3",
                                                "text": "The older man introduced himself as Otto. The other two were Fabio and Gunther. They were chiropterologists he explained from Erlangen University in Germany."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "36f81abe-3f60-4d40-954d-a85a28066de5",
                                                "sense_id": "6f0792d4-7f8a-377e-a444-d6ee85fa69f3",
                                                "text": "According to the recommendation, the chiropterologist would work in the Wildlands Conservation Division of the Austin Water Utility and would protect the population of about 1.5 million bats from disease, impacts of climate change and harm from construction and development."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
